{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">+ Datetime addition operator</span>\n","class":"manual","created":1470,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/309226","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/Datetime-addition-operator.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/Datetime-addition-operator.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"Datetime-addition-operator\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">+ Datetime addition operator</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Adds a number of milliseconds to a DATETIME\nor a DATETIME-TZ to produce another DATETIME or DATETIME-TZ.</p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Datetime-addition-operator__syntax_GC15252679065\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d33698e101\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"Datetime-addition-operator__idGDE1V32661714\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code><var class=\"keyword varname\">datetime</var> + <var class=\"keyword varname\">milliseconds</var></code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"Datetime-addition-operator__idGDE1V42661719\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code><var class=\"keyword varname\">datetime-tz</var> + <var class=\"keyword varname\">milliseconds</var></code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <dl class=\"dl parml\">\n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">datetime</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">An expression that evaluates to a DATETIME value.</dd>\n        \n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">milliseconds</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">An expression that evaluates to an integer value specifying\na number of milliseconds.</dd>\n        \n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">datetime-tz</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">An expression that evaluates to a DATETIME-TZ value.</dd>\n        \n      </dl>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Datetime-addition-operator__example_GC15272679073\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d33698e194\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">This\nexample returns the date and time exactly 24 hours later (<code class=\"ph codeph\">dtTime</code>)\nby calculating and adding the number of milliseconds in 24 hours\nto the present date and time (NOW function) and displays the result:</p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"Datetime-addition-operator__idGDE1V52661724\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>DEFINE VARIABLE dtTime AS DATETIME NO-UNDO.\nDEFINE VARIABLE iHour  AS INTEGER  NO-UNDO INITIAL 3600000.\n\n<strong class=\"ph b\">dtTime = NOW + (24 * iHour)</strong>.\n\nMESSAGE &quot;A day later: &quot; dtTime VIEW-AS ALERT-BOX.</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Datetime-addition-operator__notes_GC15282679081\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d33698e229\">Notes</h2>\n      \n      <ul class=\"ul\">\n        <li class=\"li\">To add a specific number of days and a specific number of milliseconds to a DATETIME,\n          use the <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"DATETIME-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/DATETIME-function.html\">DATETIME function</a>. For example:<table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"Datetime-addition-operator__idGDE1V72661730\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n                <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n                  <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                    <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>new-datetime = DATETIME( DATE(old-datetime) + days, \n                         MTIME(old-datetime) + milliseconds ).</code></pre>\n                  </td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody></table><p class=\"p\">The DATETIME function ensures that the time portion remains within the valid\n            range, by adding day(s) to the date part when the time part goes over the number of\n            milliseconds in a day.</p></li>\n        <li class=\"li\">To add a specific number of days and milliseconds to a DATETIME-TZ, use the <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"DATETIME-TZ-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/DATETIME-TZ-function.html\">DATETIME-TZ function</a>. For example:<table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"Datetime-addition-operator__idGDE1V82661734\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n                <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n                  <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                    <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>new-datetime-tz = DATETIME-TZ( DATE(old-datetime-tz) + days, \n                               MTIME (old-datetime-tz) + milliseconds,\n                               TIMEZONE(old-dateime-tz) ).</code></pre>\n                  </td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody></table><p class=\"p\">The DATETIME-TZ function ensures that the time portion remains within the valid\n            range, by adding day(s) to the date portion when the time part goes over the number of\n            milliseconds in a day.</p></li>\n      </ul>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Datetime-addition-operator__see-also_GC15292679089\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d33698e294\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Date-addition-operator.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Date-addition-operator.html\">+ Date addition operator</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Datetime-subtraction-operator.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Datetime-subtraction-operator.html\">- Datetime subtraction operator</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"ADD-INTERVAL-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ADD-INTERVAL-function.html\">ADD-INTERVAL function</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"DATETIME-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/DATETIME-function.html\">DATETIME function</a>, <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"DATETIME-TZ-function.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/DATETIME-TZ-function.html\">DATETIME-TZ function</a></p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Date-addition-operator.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Date-addition-operator.html\">+ Date addition operator</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Unary-negative-operator.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Unary-negative-operator.html\">- Unary negative operator</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/309226","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":1470,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"+ Datetime addition operator","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Datetime-addition-operator.html","type":"Manual"}